NAME
  useradd - create a Freax login account

SYNOPSIS
  useradd NAME

DESCRIPTION
  Creates NAME in /etc/passwd and /etc/shadow, allocates a UID and GID,
  and creates /home/NAME. The new account starts without a password; use
  `passwd NAME` or interactive `adduser NAME`.

  Requires effective UID 0. This command manages Freax login accounts,
  not Minecraft player authorization.

  A new account can write inside its own home and /tmp/<uid>. Freax has no
  per-file ownership yet, so accounts can also write inside each other's
  home directories.

EXAMPLES
  useradd alice
